    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d350">

                <pb facs="0850" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg728"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr.
                            King.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 8,
                        1889</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 29.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 33 of the 12th
                    ultimo, referring to a note verbale received in February last, from the Sublime
                    Porte, regarding the military service of cavasses and dragomans employed by
                    foreign consulates.</p>
                <p>The terms of your proposed reply to the note of February are approved. It is
                    hoped that the exemption sought for our employés, not being claimed as a right,
                    will be conceded as a favor, so that the business of our officers in Turkey may
                    not be embarrassed by the abrupt withdrawal of such experienced persons from our
                    service.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James G. Blaine.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
